Sheet Pan Gnocchi
  --Dan Pelosi (ak Grossy Pelosi)

Vinagrette:
1/4 c finely chopped fresh basil leaves
1/8 c olive oil
1 tbsp white wine or balsamic vinegar
1/2 tsp salt
Juice of 1/2 lemon

Place basil, olive oil, vinegar, salt, and lemon juice in a small mixing bowl. Whisk until well combined and set aside.

Gnocchi:
1 lb package potato gnocchi (can use cauliflower as well)
2 c cherry tomatoes
6 cloves garlic, smashed
3 tbsp olive oil
1/4 tsp freshly ground black pepper
1/2 tsp salt
1/4 tsp red pepper flakes, optional
2 heaping c arugula
1 large ball burrata cheese

Preheat oven to 425F. Place gnocchi, cherry tomatoes, garlic, olive oil, salt, pepper and red pepper flakes on a sheet pan and toss together until well combined. Spread evenly in the pan. Place sheet pan in preheated oven and bake for 20 min, giving everything on the pan a toss halfway through roasting to ensure that the gnocchi crisp evenly. Remove sheet pan from the oven and top gnocchi and tomatoes with the arugula and drizzle with the basil vinaigrette. Toss to coat evenly. Place the ball of burrata in the center of the sheet pan, and carefully break open the cheese over the top of the gnocchi. Serve immediately and enjoy!
